## 7. Delete requires an explicit confirm step — PASS (requirement met; one defect noted, see 10.2)

FIRST CLICK, no confirm token — POST /accounts/zz-check/delete with an empty
body → 200. The account was NOT deleted:

    disk after single click: ['zz-check','aa-all']

and the response renders the confirm panel instead:

    <div ... role="alert">
      <p ...>Deleting an account is destructive: its transactions become
       unassigned. This cannot be undone.</p>
      <form hx-post="/accounts/zz-check/delete" ...>
        <input type="hidden" name="confirm" value="yes">
        <button type="submit" ...>Yes, delete &ldquo;ZZ Checking&rdquo;</button>

CONFIRMED CLICK — POST /accounts/zz-check/delete with confirm=yes → 200,
occurrences of "ZZ Checking" in the response: 0, and disk: ['aa-all'].

So a single click provably cannot destroy an account; the destructive action is
gated behind a second, differently-parameterized submit. Requirement met.

