## 9. Tests assert on what the handler RENDERS — PASS (this was the highest-risk item)

The 2026-08-16a failure mode is a test that renders a DIFFERENT template than
production does. I checked template-loading parity directly rather than trusting
the test names:

    production  cmd/server/main.go:76-77
        templatesFS, _ := fs.Sub(web.EmbeddedFS, "templates")
        renderer, err = templates.NewFromFS(templatesFS, false)

    test        handlers_test.go:65-69
        templatesFS, err := fs.Sub(web.EmbeddedFS, "templates")
        rend, err := templates.NewFromFS(templatesFS, false)

Byte-identical FS root and constructor. The renderer-mode tests therefore
exercise the exact template set the server ships, closing the hole 2026-08-16a
was about.

Eight of the nineteen tests run in renderer mode and assert on markup, not on
pageData:

  - TestHandlePage_RendersFullPageInRendererMode — full page carries
    <!doctype>/<html> and an <h1>, i.e. the base layout resolved
    "accounts-content" rather than falling through to base.html's "Page Not
    Found" branch.
  - TestHandleCreate_RendererMode_SwapsAccountsListPartial — asserts the
    mutation response does NOT contain <!doctype>/<html> (it is the partial),
    DOES contain the new account name, and DOES contain
    id="accounts-list-heading". This is the direct 2026-08-16a guard: it would
    fail if the handler returned the full page or a different partial.
  - TestHandleCreate_RendererMode_ValidationErrorSurfacedInPartial — asserts
    "duplicate" text, role="alert"/aria-live, and aria-invalid="true" in the
    swapped markup.
  - TestHandleDelete_RendererMode_ConfirmPanelRendered — asserts name="confirm",
    value="yes", "Yes, delete", and that the account is still listed.
  - TestHandleDelete_RendererMode_ConfirmedDeleteRemovesAccount — asserts the
    name is absent AND that the response is still the list section.
  - TestHandleAddAnchor_RendererMode_AnchorShownInPartial — asserts the date,
    the FORMATTED amount "$4,210.55" and the note in the swapped markup.
  - Plus two page-level markup tests (labels, required/format text).

Independent corroboration: I reproduced every one of those assertions against
the live binary over HTTP (items 3-7 above), so the tests are not merely
self-consistent with a stale template — they agree with the running server.

Ruling 2026-08-16e — loop-based assertions without a preceding count assertion.
Four `for ... range` in handlers_test.go:

  - :42  ranges a string literal (fixture writing, not an assertion) — n/a.
  - :598 ranges a string literal of five field IDs; the iteration count is fixed
    by the literal and cannot be vacuously zero — n/a.
  - :762 equalStrings helper, guarded by an explicit len(a)!=len(b) check — n/a.
  - :372 `for _, v := range data.Accounts { got[v.Account.ID] = v.MatchedFiles }`
    — FLAGGED per 2026-08-16e. There is no `len(data.Accounts) != 3` assertion
    before it. It is a collect loop, not an assert loop, and the following
    positive assertion (equalStrings(got["usaa-all"], want)) does fail if the
    loop yields nothing — so it is not actually vacuous — but the two negative
    assertions at :378 and :381 (`len(got[...]) != 0`) WOULD pass vacuously on an
    empty page. Reporting as required by the ruling; non-blocking, because the
    positive assertion anchors the loop.

Test-coverage gap worth recording (non-blocking): the per-account "Matched
files" list — the headline deliverable of item 4 — is asserted only at the
pageData level (TestBuildPageData_PatternEditorListsMatchedFiles), never in
rendered HTML. The Unassigned list from the identical pipeline IS asserted in
HTML (TestHandlePage_RendererMode_UnassignedFilesShownByText, checking for
"vanguard-2026.csv"), and I verified the matched-files markup myself against the
live server (item 4a/4b), so the behavior is confirmed — but a template
regression that dropped the matched-files <ul> would not be caught by the suite.

