## 10. Notes and defects for the lead

10.1 The task brief is not present in the worktree: `.swarm/briefs/A6.md` does
not exist under .swarm/work/A6. I read it from the main tree at
/home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/.swarm/briefs/A6.md. Informational.

10.2 DEFECT (not a violation of any written requirement; recommend a follow-up
task rather than a rejection). The "Cancel" button inside the delete-confirm
panel is a dead control. Both buttons in the panel post to the same endpoint;
only the destructive one carries the token:

    <form hx-post="/accounts/aa-all/delete" ...>
      <input type="hidden" name="confirm" value="yes">
      <button type="submit" ...>Yes, delete "..."</button></form>
    <form hx-post="/accounts/aa-all/delete" ...>          <-- Cancel: no token
      <button type="submit" ...>Cancel</button></form>

handleDelete treats "no confirm token" as "open the confirm panel"
(handlers.go:172-177), so Cancel re-renders the identical panel. Verified live:
after posting the Cancel form, occurrences of "Yes, delete" in the response = 1,
i.e. the panel is still open. The user has no way to dismiss the destructive
panel short of reloading. No test covers Cancel. I did not fail the task on this
because brief requirement 7 as written is "require an explicit confirm step
rather than deleting on a single click", which is fully satisfied and proven
above — the safety property holds; only the escape hatch is broken.

10.3 DEFECT, accessibility lane (deferring the ruling to checker-a11y, recorded
here because I found it while testing item 3's error surfacing). The HTMX focus
script (accounts.html:99) does
`target.querySelector('[data-focus-target]')`, but `data-focus-target="id"`
(:165) and `data-focus-target="name"` (:182) are emitted UNCONDITIONALLY on the
create form, not gated on ErrorField. So the first match in DOM order is always
the create-form ID input. Verified live on a NAME-error response — the first
data-focus-target element in the returned partial is:

    <input type="text" id="acct-new-id" name="id" required autocomplete="off"
     data-focus-target="id" aria-describedby="acct-new-id-help" ...>

Focus therefore lands on the ID field for every error and every successful swap,
never on the offending field. Errors are still announced (the partial's
role="alert" block is newly inserted on each swap), so this is a focus-management
defect, ACCESSIBILITY.md points 5 and 10, not an announcement defect.

10.4 Observation, no action needed: pageData.Warnings and both template blocks
that render pattern-overlap warnings are unreachable — the handler calls
accounts.Save, never accounts.SaveWithWarnings, so Warnings is always empty. The
brief does not ask for overlap warnings, so this is dead UI, not a miss.

10.5 Observation: the renderer==nil JSON fallback (handlers.go:118, :534) is a
test-only branch living in production code. It is unreachable in production —
cmd/server/main.go:111 always passes a non-nil renderer — and the eight
renderer-mode tests cover the real path, so it does not weaken item 9.

